Object.assign(window.TEM8_DICTIONARY, {"riding":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/riding__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/riding__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪdɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the sport or activity of riding horses","cn":"骑马","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"I'm taking riding lessons.","cn":"我在学习骑马。"}},{"en":"one of the three former parts of the English county of Yorkshire called the East Riding, the North Riding and the West Riding","cn":"区（英格兰约克郡以前的东、北、西三个行政分区之一）","g":"[countable]"},{"en":"a district that elects its own representative to a state or national government","cn":"骑马：选出自己的州或中央政府代表的地区","g":"[countable]","lab":"Canadian English","ex":{"en":"A by-election was called for the Ontario riding of Whitby-Oshawa.","cn":"安大略省惠特比-奥沙瓦选区需要进行补选。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"骑马（运动）","en":"Riding is the activity or sport of riding horses.","ex":{"en":"The next morning we went riding again","cn":"第二天早上，我们又去骑马了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I'm taking riding lessons.","cn":"我在学习骑马。"},{"en":"( BrE ) to go riding","cn":"去骑马"}]},"rise":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rise__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rise__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"raɪz","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to come or go upwards; to reach a higher level or position","cn":"上升；攀升；提高；达到较高水平（或位置）","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"move upwards","ex":{"en":"The curtain rose to reveal an empty stage.","cn":"幕布升起，露出一个空荡荡的舞台。"}},{"en":"to increase in amount or number","cn":"（数量或数字）增加，增长，提高","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"British English","sc":"increase","ex":{"en":"Prices are still rising.","cn":"价格仍在上涨。"}},{"en":"when the sun, moon, etc. rises, it appears above the horizon","cn":"升起","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of sun/moon","ex":{"en":"The sun rises in the east.","cn":"太阳从东方升起。"}},{"en":"to become more successful, important, powerful, etc.","cn":"变得更加成功（或重要、强大等）","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"become powerful/important","ex":{"en":"a rising young politician","cn":"崭露头角的年轻政治家"}},{"en":"to get up from a lying, sitting or kneeling position","cn":"起床；起立；站起来","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"get up","ex":{"en":"He was accustomed to rising (= getting out of bed) early.","cn":"他习惯于早起。"}},{"en":"to end a meeting","cn":"休会；闭会；散会","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"end meeting","ex":{"en":"The House (= members of the House of Commons) rose at 10 p.m.","cn":"下议院于晚上 10 点钟散会。"}},{"en":"if a sound rises, it becomes louder and higher","cn":"提高；增强","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of sound","ex":{"en":"Her voice rose angrily.","cn":"她气得提高了嗓门。"}},{"en":"if the wind rises, it begins to blow more strongly","cn":"刮起来；刮得更猛","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of wind","ex":{"en":"The wind is rising—I think there's a storm coming.","cn":"风越刮越猛--大概要来暴风雨了。"}},{"en":"if a feeling rises inside you, it begins and gets stronger","cn":"增强","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"of feeling","ex":{"en":"He felt anger rising inside him.","cn":"他心里直冒火。"}},{"en":"if your colour rises, your face becomes pink or red because you are embarrassed","cn":"（因尴尬而）脸红","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"of your colour"},{"en":"if hair rises, it stands up instead of lying flat","cn":"竖起；立起来","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of hair","ex":{"en":"The hair on the back of my neck rose when I heard the scream.","cn":"听到那尖叫声，我不禁毛骨悚然。"}},{"en":"to begin to fight against your government or leader or against a foreign army","cn":"起义；反抗","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"fight","ex":{"en":"The peasants rose in revolt.","cn":"农民起来造反了。"}},{"en":"to be able to be seen above everything that is around","cn":"耸立；矗立；高耸","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","sc":"start to be seen","ex":{"en":"Mountains rose in the distance.","cn":"远处山峦叠起。"}},{"en":"if land rises, it slopes upwards","cn":"凸起；隆起","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of land","ex":{"en":"The ground rose steeply all around.","cn":"这块地方四周都是陡坡。"}},{"en":"a river rises where it begins to flow","cn":"发源","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of beginning of river","ex":{"en":"The Thames rises in the Cotswold hills.","cn":"泰晤士河发源于科茨沃尔德丘陵。"}},{"en":"when bread, cakes, etc. rise, they become larger and rounder because of the action of yeast or baking powder","cn":"发酵","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of bread/cakes"},{"en":"to come to life again","cn":"复活；再生","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"figurative","sc":"of dead person","ex":{"en":"to rise from the dead","cn":"复活"}},{"en":"an increase in an amount, a number or a level","cn":"（数量或水平的）增加，提高","g":"[countable]","sc":"increase","ex":{"en":"The industry is feeling the effects of recent price rises.","cn":"这一行业已经感觉到了最近提价的影响。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an increase in the money you are paid for the work you do","cn":"加薪；工资增长","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English","sc":"increase","ex":{"en":"I'm going to ask for a rise.","cn":"我打算要求加薪。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the act of becoming more important, successful, powerful, etc.","cn":"（重要性、优势、权力等的）增强","g":"[singular]","sc":"in power/importance","ex":{"en":"The film traces the rise of fascism in Europe.","cn":"该片记述了法西斯主义在欧洲的兴起。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a movement upwards","cn":"向上移动","g":"[singular]","lab":"British English","sc":"a movement upwards","ex":{"en":"She watched the gentle rise and fall of his chest as he slept.","cn":"她看着他睡着时微微起伏的胸膛。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an area of land that slopes upwards","cn":"斜坡；小丘；小山","g":"[countable]","sc":"sloping land","ex":{"en":"The church was built at the top of a small rise.","cn":"教堂建在一座小山顶上。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"上升;升高;升起","en":"If something rises, it moves upwards.","ex":{"en":"He watched the smoke rise from his cigarette","cn":"他注视着烟雾从香烟上升起。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"站起来","en":"When you rise, you stand up.","ex":{"en":"Luther rose slowly from the chair","cn":"卢瑟慢慢地从椅子上站起来。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"起床","en":"When you rise, you get out of bed.","ex":{"en":"Tony had risen early and gone to the cottage to work.","cn":"托尼很早就起来去小屋干活了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(太阳、月亮)升起，升空","en":"When the sun or moon rises, it appears in the sky.","ex":{"en":"He wanted to be over the line of the ridge before the sun had risen.","cn":"他想在太阳升起以前翻过山脊。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"矗立;耸立","en":"You can say that something rises when it appears as a large tall shape.","ex":{"en":"The building rose before him, tall and stately","cn":"那座高大宏伟的建筑耸立在他面前。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"升高;上升;上涨","en":"If the level of something such as the water in a river rises, it becomes higher.","ex":{"en":"The waters continue to rise as more than 1,000 people are evacuated.","cn":"水面持续上涨，已经有1,000多人被疏散了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(地面)升高，变陡","en":"If land rises, it slopes upwards.","ex":{"en":"He looked up the slope of land that rose from the house","cn":"他抬头看了看屋后的斜坡。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"上坡;斜坡","en":"A rise is an area of ground that slopes upwards.","ex":{"en":"The pub itself was on a rise, commanding views across the countryside","cn":"酒吧本身就建在一个斜坡上，可以俯眺乡村风光。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(数量)上升，增长，上涨","en":"If an amount rises, it increases.","ex":{"en":"Pre-tax profits rose from £842,000 to £1.82m","cn":"税前利润从84.2万英镑上升到了182万英镑。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(数量的)上升，增长，上涨","en":"A rise in the amount of something is an increase in it.","ex":{"en":"...the prospect of another rise in interest rates","cn":"利率可能会再次上涨"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(工资的)上涨，增加","en":"A rise is an increase in your wages or your salary.","ex":{"en":"He will get a pay rise of nearly £4,000.","cn":"他的工资将会上涨将近4,000英镑。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(运动或活动的)兴起,抬头，高涨","en":"The rise of a movement or activity is an increase in its popularity or influence.","ex":{"en":"...the rise of racism in America.","cn":"美国种族主义的抬头"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(风力)加强，增强","en":"If the wind rises, it becomes stronger.","ex":{"en":"The wind was still rising, approach-ing a force nine gale.","cn":"风力仍在增强，接近9级大风。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(声音)变大，提高","en":"If a sound rises or if someone's voice rises, it becomes louder or higher.","ex":{"en":"'Bernard?' Her voice rose hysterically","cn":"“伯纳德？”她歇斯底里地提高了嗓门。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(声音)从…传来","en":"If a sound rises from a group of people, it comes from them.","ex":{"en":"There were low, muffled voices rising from the hallway.","cn":"从走廊里隐约传来了低沉的说话声。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(感情)突然变得强烈，涌起","en":"If an emotion rises in someone, they suddenly feel it very intensely so that it affects their behaviour.","ex":{"en":"A tide of emotion rose and clouded his judgement","cn":"心头涌起一阵强烈的感情，模糊了他的判断力。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(因为生气、尴尬或兴奋)脸红，涨红脸","en":"If your colour rises or if a blush rises in your cheeks, you turn red because you feel angry, embarrassed, or excited.","ex":{"en":"Amy felt the colour rising in her cheeks at the thought.","cn":"埃米一想到这件事，就觉得脸红。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"起义;反抗;造反","en":"When the people in a country rise, they try to defeat the government or army that is controlling them.","ex":{"en":"The National Convention has promised armed support to any people who wish to rise against armed oppression.","cn":"国民议会承诺向所有想要反抗武装压迫的人提供武装支持。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"升职;升迁;地位提高;变得更成功","en":"If someone rises to a higher position or status, they become more important, successful, or powerful.","ex":{"en":"She is a strong woman who has risen to the top of a deeply sexist organisation","cn":"她是一个女强人，已经升至一个性别歧视意识根深蒂固的组织的最高层。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"升迁;日益成功;地位的提高","en":"The rise of someone is the process by which they become more important, successful, or powerful.","ex":{"en":"Haig's rise was fuelled by an all-consuming sense of patriotic duty","cn":"黑格非常强烈的爱国主义责任感使他的地位大大提高了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"引起;使发生","en":"If something gives rise to an event or situation, it causes that event or situation to happen.","ex":{"en":"Low levels of choline in the body can give rise to high blood-pressure","cn":"体内胆碱水平过低会引起高血压。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to rise to the bait→see: ; to rise to the challenge→see: ; to rise to the occasion→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：rise above rise up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He criticized the huge pay rises awarded to industry bosses.","cn":"对于给企业老板大幅度加薪，他提出了批评。"},{"en":"She rose to power in the 70s.","cn":"她于 20 世纪 70 年代掌握了大权。"}]},"rings":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of jewellery that you wear on your finger, consisting of a round band of gold, silver, etc., sometimes decorated with precious stones","cn":"戒指；指环"},{"en":"an object in the shape of a circle with a large hole in the middle","cn":"环状物；圈形的东西"}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/ring_comp.jpg","media/thumb/ring.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/ring__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ring__us_1.mp3"}},"richly":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/richly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/richly__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪtʃli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a beautiful and expensive manner","cn":"富丽堂皇地","ex":{"en":"a richly decorated room","cn":"装饰得富丽堂皇的房间"}},{"en":"used to express the fact that something has a pleasant strong colour, taste or smell","cn":"（色彩）鲜艳富丽地；（口味）醇美地；（气味）浓郁芬芳地","ex":{"en":"a richly flavoured sauce","cn":"味道很浓的调味汁"}},{"en":"in a generous way","cn":"慷慨地；大方地","ex":{"en":"She was richly rewarded for all her hard work.","cn":"她一向勤劳苦干，得到了丰厚的回报。"}},{"en":"in a way that people think is right and good","cn":"恰如其分地；理所当然地；完全地","ex":{"en":"richly deserved success","cn":"理应取得的成功"}},{"en":"used to express the fact that the quality or thing mentioned is present in large amounts","cn":"（表明品质突出或物质丰富）","ex":{"en":"richly varied countryside","cn":"各地情况迥异的乡村"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"（色彩）艳丽地，强烈地;（味道、香味）浓郁地","en":"If something is richly coloured, flavoured, or perfumed, it has a pleasantly strong colour, flavour, or perfume.","ex":{"en":"...an opulent display of richly coloured fabrics.","cn":"各种色彩艳丽的织物的华美展示"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"（装饰）精美地，华美地，华丽地","en":"If something is richly decorated, patterned, or furnished, it has a lot of elaborate and beautiful decoration, patterns, or furniture.","ex":{"en":"Coffee steamed in the richly decorated silver pot.","cn":"咖啡在装饰精美的银壶中冒着热气。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"非常;充分;完全","en":"If you say that someone richly deserves an award, success, or victory, you approve of what they have done and feel very strongly that they deserve it.","ex":{"en":"He achieved the success he so richly deserved.","cn":"他取得了自己完全应得的成功。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"充分地;丰富地","en":"If a person or place is richly endowed or supplied with something, they have a lot of it.","ex":{"en":"...a boy richly endowed with courage","cn":"一个充满勇气的男孩"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"（回报）丰厚地，令人惬意地","en":"If you are richly rewarded for doing something, you get something very valuable or pleasant in return for doing it.","ex":{"en":"It is a difficult book to read, but it richly rewards the effort","cn":"这本书很难读懂，但是非常值得一读。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She was richly rewarded for all her hard work.","cn":"她一向勤劳苦干，得到了丰厚的回报。"},{"en":"The polished floor glowed richly.","cn":"光洁无瑕的地板十分明亮。"}]},"riot":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/riot__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/riot__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪət","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which a group of people behave in a violent way in a public place, often as a protest","cn":"暴乱；骚乱","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"One prison guard was killed when a riot broke out in the jail.","cn":"一位狱警在监狱骚乱中丧生。"}},{"en":"a collection of a lot of different types of the same thing","cn":"丰富多彩；品种繁多","g":"[singular]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"The garden was a riot of colour.","cn":"花园里色彩缤纷。"}},{"en":"a person or an event that is very funny","cn":"活宝；笑料","g":"[singular]","lab":"old-fashioned, informal，，","ex":{"en":"The movie is a laugh riot.","cn":"这部电影很搞笑。"}},{"en":"to behave in a violent way in a public place, often as a protest","cn":"发生骚乱；闹事","ex":{"en":"Students all over the country rioted against the government.","cn":"全国各地的学生骚乱反对政府。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"暴乱;骚动;暴动","en":"When there is a riot, a crowd of people behave violently in a public place, for example they fight, throw stones, or damage buildings and vehicles.","ex":{"en":"Twelve inmates have been killed during a riot at the prison.","cn":"12名犯人在一场监狱暴乱中被杀害。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"闹事;发动暴乱","en":"If people riot, they behave violently in a public place.","ex":{"en":"Last year 600 inmates rioted, starting fires and building barricades","cn":"去年，600名犯人闹事，他们纵火并设置路障。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"五颜六色;丰富多彩;各种各样","en":"If you say that there is a riot of something pleasant such as colour, you mean that there is a large amount of various types of it.","ex":{"en":"All the cacti were in flower, so that the desert was a riot of colour","cn":"所有的仙人掌都开花了，整个沙漠里五彩缤纷。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"严厉警告…停止闹事;严厉警告…注意言行","en":"If someone in authority reads you the riot act, they tell you that you will be punished unless you start behaving properly.","ex":{"en":"I'm glad you read the riot act to Billy. He's still a kid and still needs to be told what to do.","cn":"我很高兴你警告比利不许胡闹。他还是个孩子，仍然需要有人告诉他该做什么。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"失去控制;变得狂乱;无法无天","en":"If people run riot, they behave in a wild and uncontrolled manner.","ex":{"en":"Rampaging prisoners ran riot through Strangeways jail.","cn":"斯特兰韦斯监狱里那些狂暴的囚犯们全都失去了控制。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(想象力等)狂野，不受拘束，任意发挥","en":"If something such as your imagination runs riot, it is not limited or controlled, and produces ideas that are new or exciting, rather than sensible.","ex":{"en":"A conservatory offers the perfect excuse to let your imagination run riot.","cn":"音乐学院让你有充分的理由任想象力自由驰骋。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"One prison guard was killed when a riot broke out in the jail.","cn":"一位狱警在监狱骚乱中丧生。"},{"en":"They let their kids run riot.","cn":"他们听任自己的孩子撒野。"}]},"rid":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rid__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( formal ) to be free of sb/sth that has been annoying you or that you do not want","cn":"摆脱"},{"en":"to make yourself free of sb/sth that is annoying you or that you do not want; to throw sth away","cn":"摆脱；丢弃；扔掉"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"扔掉;丢弃","en":"When you get rid of something that you do not want or do not like, you take action so that you no longer have it or suffer from it.","ex":{"en":"The owner needs to get rid of the car for financial reasons","cn":"因为经济原因，车主必须把汽车处理掉。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"摆脱;甩掉;赶走","en":"If you get rid of someone who is causing problems for you or who you do not like, you do something to prevent them affecting you any more, for example by making them leave.","ex":{"en":"He believed that his manager wanted to get rid of him for personal reasons","cn":"他认为经理是出于个人原因想开除他。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"使…去掉;使…去除;使…摆脱","en":"If you rid a place or person of something undesirable or unwanted, you succeed in removing it completely from that place or person.","ex":{"en":"The proposals are an attempt to rid the country of political corruption","cn":"这些提议试图使这个国家摆脱政治腐败。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"摆脱;去除;消除","en":"If you rid yourself of something you do not want, you take action so that you no longer have it or are no longer affected by it.","ex":{"en":"Why couldn't he ever rid himself of those thoughts, those worries?","cn":"为什么他总是无法摆脱那些想法和担忧?"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"得到解脱的;摆脱…的","en":"If you are rid of someone or something that you did not want or that caused problems for you, they are no longer with you or causing problems for you.","ex":{"en":"The family had sought a way to be rid of her and the problems she had caused them.","cn":"这家人已经找到一个方法摆脱她以及她给他们带来的问题。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"幸亏摆脱了","en":"If you say that someone is well rid of someone, you think it is good that the person has gone because you did not like them or you think they caused a lot of problems.","ex":{"en":"It seems to me your wife was a shallow woman and you're well rid of her.","cn":"在我看来你妻子是一个浅薄的女人，幸好你离开了她。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"( BrE ) He was a nuisance and we're all well rid of him (= we'll be much better without him).","cn":"他这人很讨厌，没有他我们都会舒服得多。"},{"en":"Try and get rid of your visitors before I get there.","cn":"在我到达之前，想办法把你的客人打发走。"}]},"rides":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( formal ) to be free of sb/sth that has been annoying you or that you do not want","cn":"摆脱"},{"en":"to make yourself free of sb/sth that is annoying you or that you do not want; to throw sth away","cn":"摆脱；丢弃；扔掉"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rid__us_1.mp3"}},"ridicule":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ridicule__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ridicule__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪdɪkjuːl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"unkind comments that make fun of somebody/something or make them look silly","cn":"嘲笑；奚落；讥笑","ex":{"en":"She is an object of ridicule in the tabloid newspapers.","cn":"她是小报讥笑讽刺的对象。"}},{"en":"to make somebody/something look silly by laughing at them or it in an unkind way","cn":"嘲笑；奚落；讥笑","ex":{"en":"They ridicule the president as a man who has lost control of events.","cn":"他们嘲笑总统是一个失去了对事态控制的人。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"嘲笑;奚落;嘲弄","en":"If you ridicule someone or ridicule their ideas or beliefs, you make fun of them in an unkind way.","ex":{"en":"I admired her all the more for allowing them to ridicule her and never striking back","cn":"她能听任他们嘲笑却从不还击，这让我更加敬佩她。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"嘲笑;奚落;嘲弄","en":"If someone or something is an object of ridicule or is held up to ridicule, someone makes fun of them in an unkind way.","ex":{"en":"As a heavy child, she became the object of ridicule from classmates","cn":"由于体胖，她成了班上同学嘲笑的对象。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She is an object of ridicule in the tabloid newspapers.","cn":"她是小报讥笑讽刺的对象。"},{"en":"to hold sb up to ridicule (= make fun of sb publicly)","cn":"公然取笑某人"}]},"ribbon":{"media":{"img":["media/pic/rope_comp.jpg","media/thumb/ribbon.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/ribbon__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ribbon__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪbən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a narrow piece of material, used to tie things or for decoration","cn":"（用于捆绑或装饰的）带子，丝带","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"Her present was tied with yellow ribbon.","cn":"她的礼物上系着黄丝带。"}},{"en":"something that is long and narrow in shape","cn":"带状物；狭长的东西","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The road was a ribbon of moonlight.","cn":"这条路在月光下如同一条缎带。"}},{"en":"a ribbon in special colours, or tied in a special way, that is given to somebody as a prize or as a military honour, or that is worn by somebody to show that they belong to a particular political party","cn":"绶带；勋带","g":"[countable]"},{"en":"a long narrow piece of material containing ink (= coloured liquid for writing, drawing, etc.) that you put into typewriters and some computer printers","cn":"（打字机或某些打印机的）色带","g":"[countable]"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"（用作捆绑或装饰的）缎带，丝带","en":"A ribbon is a long, narrow piece of cloth that you use for tying things together or as a decoration.","ex":{"en":"She had tied back her hair with a peach satin ribbon.","cn":"她用一根桃色缎带把头发扎在脑后。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(打字机或打印机的)色带","en":"A typewriter or printer ribbon is a long, narrow piece of cloth containing ink and is used in a typewriter or printer."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"（用以表示奖励或与某组织有关系的）绶带，勋带","en":"A ribbon is a small decorative strip of cloth which is given to someone to wear on their clothes as an award or to show that they are linked with a particular organization."}]},"examples":[{"en":"She was wearing two blue silk ribbons in her hair.","cn":"她的头发上系着两根蓝色丝带。"},{"en":"The road was a ribbon of moonlight.","cn":"这条路在月光下如同一条缎带。"}]},"rink":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"溜冰场;旱冰场","en":"A rink is a large area covered with ice where people go to ice-skate, or a large area of concrete where people go to roller-skate.","ex":{"en":"The other skaters were ordered off the rink.","cn":"其他的溜冰者都被勒令离开溜冰场。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rink__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rink__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪŋk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a specially prepared flat surface of ice, where you can ice-skate; a building where there is an ice rink","cn":"溜冰场；冰球场；溜冰馆"},{"en":"an area or a building where you can roller skate","cn":"旱冰场；旱冰馆"}]}},"ringing":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪŋɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"loud and clear","cn":"响亮的；清晰的","ex":{"en":"a ringing voice","cn":"金嗓子"}},{"en":"powerful and made with a lot of force","cn":"有力的；强劲的","ex":{"en":"a ringing endorsement of her leadership","cn":"对她的领导的有力支持"}},{"en":"an act or a sound of ringing","cn":"嗡嗡作响；嗡嗡声","ex":{"en":"There was an unpleasant ringing in my ears.","cn":"我的耳朵里有一种烦人的嗡嗡声。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"响亮的;洪亮的;嘹亮的","en":"A ringing sound is loud and can be heard very clearly.","ex":{"en":"He hit the metal steps with a ringing crash.","cn":"只听他咣当一声，摔在了金属台阶上。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(声明或宣言)强有力的，铿锵有力的，令人印象深刻的","en":"A ringing statement or declaration is one that is made forcefully and is intended to make a powerful impression.","ex":{"en":"So far we have had ringing declarations, but only limited action.","cn":"目前，我们已经发表了一些有力的声明，但只采取了有限的行动。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ringing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ringing__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"There was an unpleasant ringing in my ears.","cn":"我的耳朵里有一种烦人的嗡嗡声。"},{"en":"a ringing endorsement of her leadership","cn":"对她的领导的有力支持"}]},"rising":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rising__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rising__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪzɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which a group of people protest against, and try to get rid of, a government, a leader, etc.","cn":"起义；叛乱","ex":{"en":"The rising was crushed by government troops.","cn":"起义被政府军镇压。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Francesca was a rising star in the cinema.","cn":"弗朗西丝卡是影坛新星。"},{"en":"The rising generation of students are optimistic about the future.","cn":"年轻一代的学生对未来很乐观。"}]},"right":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/right__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/right__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"raɪt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"true or correct as a fact","cn":"正确的；真正的；真实的","lab":"informal","sc":"true/correct","ex":{"en":"Did you get the answer right?","cn":"你回答得正确吗？"}},{"en":"correct in your opinion or judgement","cn":"（意见或判断）准确，确切，恰当","g":"[not before noun]","sc":"true/correct","ex":{"en":"You were quite right about the weather.","cn":"你对天气的预测很准确。"}},{"en":"correct for a particular situation or thing, or for a particular person","cn":"适当的；正好的；恰当的","sc":"true/correct","ex":{"en":"Have you got the right money (= the exact amount) for the bus fare?","cn":"你有数额刚好的零钱付公交车车费吗？"}},{"en":"morally good or acceptable; correct according to law or a person’s duty","cn":"正当；妥当","g":"[not usually before noun]","sc":"morally good","ex":{"en":"I hope we're doing the right thing.","cn":"我希望我们这样做是妥当的。"}},{"en":"in a normal or good enough condition","cn":"正常；情况良好","g":"[not before noun]","lab":"offensive","sc":"normal","ex":{"en":"I don't feel quite right today (= I feel ill).","cn":"我今天感觉不太舒服。"}},{"en":"socially fashionable or important","cn":"符合潮流的；有社会地位的","sc":"fashionable/important","ex":{"en":"She knows all the right people (= for example, people who can help her in her career).","cn":"她认识所有大人物。"}},{"en":"of, on or towards the side of the body that is towards the east when a person faces north","cn":"右边的","g":"[only before noun]","sc":"not left","ex":{"en":"your right hand/arm/foot/leg","cn":"右手；右臂；右脚；右腿"}},{"en":"used to emphasize something bad","cn":"（强调坏事）真正的，完全的","g":"[only before noun]","lab":"British English, informal, especially disapproving，，，，","sc":"complete","ex":{"en":"You made a right mess of that!","cn":"你把这件事完全给弄糟了！"}},{"en":"on or to the right side","cn":"在右边；向右边","sc":"not left","ex":{"en":"Turn right at the end of the street.","cn":"在街的那头往右拐。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"exactly; directly","cn":"正好；恰好；直接地","sc":"exactly","ex":{"en":"Lee was standing right behind her.","cn":"李就站在她身后。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"all the way; completely","cn":"一直；径直；完全地","sc":"completely","ex":{"en":"They drove right up to the door.","cn":"他们一直开到门口。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"immediately; without delay","cn":"立即；马上；毫不耽搁","sc":"immediately","ex":{"en":"I'll be right back.","cn":"我马上就回来。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"correctly","cn":"正确","sc":"correctly","ex":{"en":"You guessed right.","cn":"你猜着了。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"in the way that things should happen or are supposed to happen; in a way that is morally good","cn":"顺利；正常；正当","lab":"North American English","sc":"in a good way","ex":{"en":"Nothing's going right for me today.","cn":"今天没有哪一件事让我顺心。"},"pos":"adverb"},{"en":"the right side or direction","cn":"右边；右方；右","g":"[singular]","sc":"not left side","ex":{"en":"Take the first street on the right.","cn":"走右手的第一条街。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the first, second, etc. road on the right side","cn":"右边的（第一条、第二条等）路","g":"[singular]","sc":"not left side","ex":{"en":"Take the first right, then the second left.","cn":"在第一个路口向右拐，然后再在第二个路口向左拐。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a turn to the right","cn":"右拐；右转弯","g":"[singular]","lab":"North American English also","sc":"not left side","ex":{"en":"Take a right at the traffic lights.","cn":"在红绿灯处右转。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a moral or legal claim to have or get something or to behave in a particular way","cn":"正当的要求；权利","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"moral/legal claim","ex":{"en":"They had fought hard for equal rights.","cn":"他们为了获得平等权利已经进行了顽强的斗争。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"what is morally good or correct","cn":"正当；公正；正义；正确","g":"[uncountable, countable]","sc":"something morally good","ex":{"en":"She doesn't understand the difference between right and wrong.","cn":"她不能明辨是非。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the authority to perform, publish, film, etc. a particular work, event, etc.","cn":"版权；发行权","g":"[plural]","sc":"for book/movie, etc.","ex":{"en":"He sold the rights for $2 million.","cn":"他以 200 万美元的价格出售了版权。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"political groups that most strongly support the capitalist system; part of a political party whose members are most conservative","cn":"右翼；右派","g":"[singular + singular or plural verb]","sc":"politics","ex":{"en":"The Right made great gains in the recent elections.","cn":"右翼在最近的选举中大获全胜。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a hard hit that is made with your right hand","cn":"右手拳","g":"[countable]","sc":"in boxing","pos":"noun"},{"en":"to return somebody/something/yourself to the normal position, standing or sitting upright","cn":"使回到正常位置；把…扶正；使…直立","sc":"return to position","ex":{"en":"They learnt to right a capsized canoe.","cn":"他们学会了将倾覆的独木舟翻过来。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to correct something that is wrong or not in its normal state","cn":"改正；纠正；使恢复正常","sc":"correct","ex":{"en":"Righting the economy will demand major cuts in expenditure.","cn":"恢复经济需要大量削减开支。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"used to show that you accept a statement or an order","cn":"（表示同意或遵从）是的，好的","lab":"old-fashioned","ex":{"en":"‘You may find it hurts a little at first.’ ‘Right.’","cn":"“开始时，你会觉得有点疼。”“噢。”"},"pos":"exclamation"},{"en":"used to get somebody’s attention to say that you are ready to do something, or to tell them to do something","cn":"（引起注意，表示已做好准备或让别人做某事）嗨，喂","ex":{"en":"Right! Let's get going.","cn":"行了！我们走吧。"},"pos":"exclamation"},{"en":"used to check that somebody agrees with you or has understood you","cn":"（要确保对方同意或明白时说）对不","ex":{"en":"So that's twenty of each sort, right?","cn":"那么，每一种都是二十个，对不对？"},"pos":"exclamation"},{"en":"used to say that you do not believe somebody or that you disagree with them","cn":"（表示不相信或不同意）是吗，好哇","lab":"ironic","ex":{"en":"‘I won't be late tonight.’ ‘Yeah, right.’","cn":"“今天晚上我不会晚的。”“是么，好哇。”"},"pos":"exclamation"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"对的;正确的;符合事实的","en":"If something is right, it is correct and agrees with the facts.","ex":{"en":"That's absolutely right","cn":"那绝对正确。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"合适的;恰当的;准确的","en":"If you do something in the right way or in the right place, you do it as or where it should be done or was planned to be done.","ex":{"en":"Walking, done in the right way, is a form of aerobic exercise","cn":"走路，如果方法正确的话，也是一种有氧健身运动。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(地方)为大众接受的;(人)正派的，体面的","en":"If you say that someone is seen in all the right places or knows all the right people, you mean that they go to places which are socially acceptable or know people who are socially acceptable.","ex":{"en":"He was always to be seen in the right places","cn":"他总是会出现在一些体面的地方。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(说法或想法)正确的，对的","en":"If someone is right about something, they are correct in what they say or think about it.","ex":{"en":"Ron has been right about the result of every General Election but one","cn":"罗恩对于历届大选结果都预测对了，只有一次除外。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(选择、行动、决定等)正确的，最好的，最合适的","en":"If something such as a choice, action, or decision is the right one, it is the best or most suitable one.","ex":{"en":"She'd made the right choice in leaving New York","cn":"她离开纽约的决定是正确的。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"正常的;没有问题的;令人满意的","en":"If something is not right, there is something unsatisfactory about the situation or thing that you are talking about.","ex":{"en":"Ratatouille doesn't taste right with any other oil","cn":"普罗旺斯杂烩用其他任何油炒出来的味道都不正宗。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"对的;正当的;有理的;合乎道德的","en":"If you think that someone was right to do something, you think that there were good moral reasons why they did it.","ex":{"en":"You were right to do what you did, under the circumstances","cn":"在这种情况下，你做的是对的。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(活动或行动)符合道德的，正当的","en":"Right is used to refer to activities or actions that are considered to be morally good and acceptable.","ex":{"en":"It's not right, leaving her like this","cn":"就这样离开她是不对的。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"扭转;矫正;(使)恢复正常","en":"If you right something or if it rights itself, it returns to its normal or correct state, after being in an undesirable state.","ex":{"en":"They recognise the urgency of righting the economy","cn":"他们认识到了复苏经济的紧迫性。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"纠正;改正;弥补","en":"If you right a wrong, you do something to make up for a mistake or something bad that you did in the past.","ex":{"en":"We've made progress in righting the wrongs of the past","cn":"我们在纠正过去的错误方面取得了进展。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把…扶正;把…摆正;(使)直立","en":"If you right something that has fallen or rolled over, or if it rights itself, it returns to its normal upright position.","ex":{"en":"He righted the yacht and continued the race","cn":"他调正了快艇，继续比赛。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(材料)正面的","en":"The right side of a material is the side that is intended to be seen and that faces outwards when it is made into something."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"进展顺利;发展正常","en":"If you say that things are going right, you mean that your life or a situation is developing as you intended or expected and you are pleased with it.","ex":{"en":"I can't think of anything in my life that's going right","cn":"我想不起我的生活中有任何一帆风顺的事情。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(道德上或法律上)有理的，合理的，正确的，说得通的","en":"If someone has behaved in a way which is morally or legally right, you can say that they are in the right. You usually use this expression when the person is involved in an argument or dispute.","ex":{"en":"She wasn't entirely in the right","cn":"她并非完全占理。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"纠正;更正","en":"If you put something right, you correct something that was wrong or that was causing problems.","ex":{"en":"We've discovered what's gone wrong and are going to put it right.","cn":"我们已经发现了存在的问题，准备加以纠正。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"白马王子;梦中情人;理想的伴侣","en":"You can use Mr Right ,Miss Right, or Ms Right to talk about the kind of person that you imagine you will marry or spend the rest of your life with.","ex":{"en":"She confesses to having trouble finding Mr Right.","cn":"她承认找不到自己的白马王子。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"heart in the right place→see: ; it serves you right→see: ; on the right side of→see: ;"},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"右边;右侧;右面","en":"The right is one of two opposite directions, sides, or positions. If you are facing north and you turn to the right, you will be facing east. In the word 'to', the 'o' is to the right of the 't'.","ex":{"en":"Ahead of you on the right will be a lovely garden","cn":"在你右前方会有一个美丽的花园。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"右边的;右侧的","en":"Your right arm, leg, or ear, for example, is the one which is on the right side of your body. Your right shoe or glove is the one which is intended to be worn on your right foot or hand."},{"pos":"N-SING-COLL 单数集合名词","cn":"右翼分子;右翼政党","en":"You can refer to people who support the political ideals of capitalism and conservatism as the right. They are often contrasted with the left, who support the political ideals of socialism.","ex":{"en":"The Tory Right despise him","cn":"保守党右翼分子鄙视他。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"（政治上的）右翼","en":"If you say that someone has moved to the right, you mean that their political beliefs have become more right-wing.","ex":{"en":"They see the shift to the right as a worldwide phenomenon.","cn":"他们认为政治上的右翼倾向是一个世界现象。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"是…的得力助手;是…的左膀右臂","en":"If someone is at a person's right hand, they work closely with that person so they can help and advise them.","ex":{"en":"I think he ought to be at the right hand of the president.","cn":"我想他应该成为总统的得力助手。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"权利;权益","en":"Your rights are what you are morally or legally entitled to do or to have.","ex":{"en":"They don't know their rights","cn":"他们不知道自己的权利。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"（做某事或拥有某物的）权利","en":"If you have a right to do or to have something, you are morally or legally entitled to do it or to have it.","ex":{"en":"...a woman's right to choose","cn":"女性的选择权"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"版权;改编权","en":"If someone has the rights to a story or book, they are legally allowed to publish it or reproduce it in another form, and nobody else can do so without their permission.","ex":{"en":"An agent bought the rights to his life","cn":"一个经纪人购买了他的传记的出版权。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"按理说;按道理","en":"If something is not the case but you think that it should be, you can say that by rights it should be the case.","ex":{"en":"She did work which by rights should be done by someone else.","cn":"她做了理应由别人做的事情。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"靠自己努力;凭借自身才能","en":"If someone is a successful or respected person in their own right, they are successful or respected because of their own efforts and talents rather than those of the people they are closely connected with.","ex":{"en":"Although now a celebrity in her own right, actress Lynn Redgrave knows the difficulties of living in the shadow of her famous older sister","cn":"虽然女演员琳恩·雷德格雷夫现在依靠自己的能力出了名，但她明白生活在大名鼎鼎的姐姐的阴影里有多不容易。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"保留…的权利","en":"If you say that you reserve the right to do something, you mean that you will do it if you feel that it is necessary.","ex":{"en":"He reserved the right to change his mind","cn":"他保留了改变主意的权利。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"在…的权限之内;有权","en":"If you say that someone is within their rights to do something, you mean that they are morally or legally entitled to do it.","ex":{"en":"You were quite within your rights to refuse to co-operate with him.","cn":"你完全有权拒绝跟他合作。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(用于引起注意或表示已经完成一件事情，接下来可以开始另一件事情)好的，对","en":"You use right in order to attract someone's attention or to indicate that you have dealt with one thing so you can go on to another.","ex":{"en":"Right, I'll be back in a minute","cn":"好的，我一会儿就回来。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"（用于确认所说的话是否正确）对吗，是吗，对吧","en":"You can use right to check whether what you have just said is correct.","ex":{"en":"They have a small plane, right?","cn":"他们有一架小飞机，对吧？"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(用于表示倾听某人的话并表示接受或理解)嗯，对，是","en":"You can say 'right' to show that you are listening to what someone is saying and that you accept it or understand it.","ex":{"en":"'Your children may well come away speaking with a bit of a broad country accent' — 'Right.' — 'because they're mixing with country children.'","cn":"“你的孩子们走的时候可能会带点儿浓重的乡下口音。”——“嗯。”——“因为他们现在和乡下孩子打成一片。”"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"好极了;对极了","en":"You say 'right on' to express your support or approval.","ex":{"en":"He suggested that many of the ideas just would not work. But the tenor of his input was 'Right on! Please show us how to make them work'.","cn":"他认为这些想法有很多根本就不会奏效。但是他说话的大意却是“好极了！请告诉我们怎么让它们见效”。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"好的;没问题","en":"If someone says 'right you are', they are agreeing to do something in a very willing and happy way.","ex":{"en":"'I want a word with you when you stop.' — 'Right you are.'","cn":"“等你停下来的时候，我想跟你说句话。”——“好的。”"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(地方、位置或时间)准确地，恰当地，精确地","en":"You can use right to emphasize the precise place, position, or time of something.","ex":{"en":"The back of a car appeared right in front of him.","cn":"汽车尾部正对着他。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"直到;一直到;径直","en":"You can use right to emphasize how far something moves or extends or how long it continues.","ex":{"en":"...the highway that runs through the Indian zone right to the army positions","cn":"穿过印第安人居住区直达军队阵地的公路"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"完全地;彻底地","en":"You can use right to emphasize that an action or state is complete.","ex":{"en":"The candle had burned right down","cn":"这根蜡烛完全烧尽了。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"完全的;彻头彻尾的;严重的","en":"You can use right to emphasize a noun, usually a noun referring to something bad.","ex":{"en":"He gave them a right telling off","cn":"他狠狠地责备了他们一通。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"就在…之后/就在…之前","en":"If you say that something happened right after a particular time or event or right before it, you mean that it happened immediately after or before it.","ex":{"en":"All of a sudden, right after the summer, Mother gets married","cn":"突然，刚过夏天，妈妈就结婚了。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"我马上就到/我马上回来","en":"If you say I'll be right there or I'll be right back, you mean that you will get to a place or get back to it in a very short time.","ex":{"en":"I'm going to get some water. I'll be right back.","cn":"我去拿点水。马上就回来。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"立刻;立即;马上","en":"If you do something right away or right off, you do it immediately.","ex":{"en":"He wants to see you right away","cn":"他想马上见你。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"现在;此时此刻","en":"You can use right now to emphasize that you are referring to the present moment.","ex":{"en":"Right now I'm feeling very excited","cn":"现在，我觉得非常激动。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"（用于英国的某些尊称中，表示级别或地位高）","en":"Right is used in some British titles. It indicates high rank or status.","ex":{"en":"...The Right Reverend John Baker.","cn":"约翰·贝克牧师阁下"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Let me get this right (= understand correctly) — you want us to do an extra ten hours' work for no extra pay?","cn":"让我先搞清楚这一点，你想让我们加班十个小时而不给加班费，是不是？"},{"en":"‘What's the right time? ’ ‘10.37.’ “","cn":"现在的准确时间是几点？” “ 10 点 37 分。”"}]},"rider":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪdə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who rides a horse, bicycle or motorcycle","cn":"骑手；骑马（或自行车、摩托车）的人","ex":{"en":"Three riders (= people riding horses) were approaching.","cn":"三个骑马的人越来越近。"}},{"en":"an extra piece of information that is added to an official document","cn":"公文的附加材料；附文","ex":{"en":"He finally agreed to a divorce with the rider that she could not remarry.","cn":"他最终同意与骑手离婚，她不能再婚。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"骑师;骑手;骑马(或自行车、摩托车)的人","en":"A rider is someone who rides a horse, a bicycle, or a motorcycle as a hobby or job. You can also refer to someone who is riding a horse, a bicycle, or a motorcycle as a rider.","ex":{"en":"She is a very good and experienced rider","cn":"她是一位经验丰富的优秀骑师。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"附文;附件;附加条款","en":"A rider is a statement that is added to another statement, especially one which contains a change, an explanation, or further information.","ex":{"en":"Mr Casey said he could see no necessity to add any rider on the use of firearms by police","cn":"凯西先生说他觉得没有必要增加任何有关警察使用枪支的附加条款。"}}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/equestriansports_comp.jpg","media/thumb/showjumping.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/rider__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rider__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Three riders (= people riding horses) were approaching.","cn":"三个骑马的人越来越近。"},{"en":"She's an experienced rider.","cn":"她是位有经验的骑手。"}]},"rivalries":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪvlri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a state in which two people, companies, etc. are competing for the same thing","cn":"竞争；竞赛；较量"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rivalry__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rivalry__us_1.mp3"}},"ring":{"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/ring.jpg","media/pic/ring_comp.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/ring__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ring__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a piece of jewellery that you wear on your finger, consisting of a round band of gold, silver, etc., sometimes decorated with precious stones","cn":"戒指；指环","g":"[countable]","sc":"jewellery","ex":{"en":"a gold ring","cn":"金戒指"}},{"en":"an object in the shape of a circle with a large hole in the middle","cn":"环状物；圈形的东西","g":"[countable]","sc":"circle","ex":{"en":"a key ring","cn":"钥匙环"}},{"en":"a round mark or shape","cn":"圆形标记；圆形","g":"[countable]","sc":"circle","ex":{"en":"She had dark rings around her eyes from lack of sleep.","cn":"她因为缺觉，眼圈儿都黑了。"}},{"en":"an area in which animals or people perform or compete, with seats around the outside for the audience","cn":"圆形表演场；圆形竞技场","g":"[countable]","sc":"for performance/competition","ex":{"en":"a boxing ring","cn":"拳击场"}},{"en":"a small flat place on a cooker that is heated by gas or electricity and is used for cooking on","cn":"炉口；灶盘","g":"[countable]","lab":"especially British English","sc":"for cooking","ex":{"en":"to turn off the gas ring","cn":"关上煤气灶"}},{"en":"a group of people who are working together, especially in secret or illegally","cn":"（尤指秘密的或非法的）团伙，帮派，集团","g":"[countable]","sc":"group of people","ex":{"en":"a spy ring","cn":"间谍网"}},{"en":"to surround somebody/something","cn":"包围；环绕","g":"[often passive]","sc":"surround","ex":{"en":"Thousands of demonstrators ringed the building.","cn":"成千上万的示威者包围了大楼。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to put a metal ring around a bird’s leg so that it can be easily identified in the future","cn":"给…戴上金属环（以便将来辨认）","sc":"bird’s leg","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to draw a circle around something","cn":"绕…画圆；把…圈起来","lab":"especially British English","sc":"draw circle","ex":{"en":"Ring the correct answer in pencil.","cn":"用铅笔圈出正确答案。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to phone somebody/something","cn":"给…打电话","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","lab":"British English","sc":"telephone","ex":{"en":"I'll ring you up later.","cn":"我稍后再给你打电话。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make a sound because somebody is trying to phone you","cn":"发出铃声","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"telephone","ex":{"en":"Will you answer the telephone if it rings?","cn":"电话铃响时你接一下好吗？"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"if you ring a bell or if a bell rings, it produces a sound","cn":"（使）发出钟声，响起铃声","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"bell","ex":{"en":"Someone was ringing the doorbell.","cn":"有人在按门铃。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be full of a sound; to fill a place with sound","cn":"回响；响彻","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"literary","sc":"with sound","ex":{"en":"The house rang with children's laughter.","cn":"房子里回响着孩子们的笑声。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be full of a particular quality","cn":"充满","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"with quality","ex":{"en":"His words rang with pride.","cn":"他的话充满了骄傲。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be uncomfortable and be unable to hear clearly, usually because you have heard a loud noise, etc.","cn":"嗡嗡作响","g":"[intransitive]","sc":"of ears","ex":{"en":"The music was so loud it made my ears ring.","cn":"音乐的声音太大了，震得我的耳朵嗡嗡响。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"the sound that a bell makes; the act of ringing a bell","cn":"铃声；钟声；摇铃；敲钟","g":"[countable]","sc":"of bell","ex":{"en":"There was a ring at the door.","cn":"门铃响了。"}},{"en":"a loud, clear sound","cn":"清晰的响声","g":"[singular]","sc":"sound","ex":{"en":"the ring of horse’s hooves on the cobblestones","cn":"马蹄在鹅卵石上发出的清脆响声"}},{"en":"a particular quality that words, sounds, etc. have","cn":"（言语、声音等的）特性","g":"[singular]","sc":"quality","ex":{"en":"His explanation has a ring of truth about it.","cn":"他的解释听上去真实可信。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"给…打电话","en":"When you ring someone, you telephone them.","ex":{"en":"He rang me at my mother's","cn":"他打电话到我妈妈家找我。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(电话)响铃，鸣响","en":"When a telephone rings, it makes a sound to let you know that someone is phoning you.","ex":{"en":"As soon as he got home, the phone rang","cn":"他一回到家，电话就响了。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(铃)作响;摇(铃);按(铃)","en":"When you ring a bell or when a bell rings, it makes a sound.","ex":{"en":"He heard the school bell ring","cn":"他听见学校的铃声响了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"按铃呼唤;摇铃召唤","en":"If you ring for something, you ring a bell to call someone to bring it to you. If you ring for someone, you ring a bell so that they will come to you.","ex":{"en":"Shall I ring for a fresh pot of tea?","cn":"要我按铃叫一壶新沏的茶水吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(声音)回响，回荡，响彻","en":"If you say that a place is ringing with sound, usually pleasant sound, you mean that the place is completely filled with that sound.","ex":{"en":"The whole place was ringing with music.","cn":"整个地方都回荡着音乐。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(说法、讨论、辩论等的)特性，特点","en":"You can use ring to describe a quality that something such as a statement, discussion, or argument seems to have. For example, if an argument has a familiar ring, it seems familiar.","ex":{"en":"His proud boast of leading 'the party of low taxation' has a hollow ring.","cn":"他洋洋得意地吹嘘自己领导着“一个主张低税收的政党”，这听起来很空洞。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"改变;改善;推出新花样","en":"If you say that someone rings the changes, you mean that they make changes or improvements to the way something is organized or done.","ex":{"en":"Ring the changes by adding spices, dried fruit or olives.","cn":"加点香料、干果或橄榄以换换口味。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"记忆犹新;在耳边回响;在脑海中浮现","en":"If you say that someone's words ring in your ears or ring in your head, you mean that you remember them very clearly, usually when you would prefer to forget them.","ex":{"en":"She shivered as the sound of that man's abuse rang in her ears.","cn":"她耳边回响起那个男人的辱骂气得浑身发抖。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"给…打电话","en":"If you give someone a ring, you phone them.","ex":{"en":"We'll give him a ring as soon as we get back.","cn":"我们一回来就会给他打电话。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(说法)听起来真实/听起来空洞","en":"If a statement rings true, it seems to be true or genuine. If it rings hollow, it does not seem to be true or genuine.","ex":{"en":"Joanna's denial rang true","cn":"乔安娜的否认听起来像是真的。"}},{"pos":"See also:","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：ring around ring back ring in ring off ring out ring round ring up"},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"戒指;指环","en":"A ring is a small circle of metal or other substance that you wear on your finger as jewellery.","ex":{"en":"She wore several diamond rings.","cn":"她戴了好几个钻石戒指。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"圈形物;环状物","en":"An object or substance that is in the shape of a circle can be described as a ring .","ex":{"en":"Frank took a large ring of keys from his pocket.","cn":"弗兰克从口袋里掏出一大串钥匙。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"围成一圈的人（或物）","en":"A group of people or things arranged in a circle can be described as a ring .","ex":{"en":"They then formed a ring around the square.","cn":"然后他们在广场周围围成了一圈。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"环形灶盘;炉头","en":"A gas or electric ring is one of the small flat areas on top of a stove which heat up and which you use for cooking."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"圆形竞技（或表演）场地;拳击台;摔跤台;马戏台","en":"At a boxing or wrestling match or a circus, the ring is the place where the contest or performance takes place. It consists of an enclosed space with seats round it.","ex":{"en":"He will never again be allowed inside a British boxing ring.","cn":"他被永久禁止踏入英国拳击赛场。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"团伙;帮派","en":"You can refer to an organized group of people who are involved in an illegal activity as a ring .","ex":{"en":"Police are investigating the suspected drug ring at the school.","cn":"警方正在调查这所学校的可疑贩毒团伙。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(建筑物或地方)用…围起来，被…环绕","en":"If a building or place is ringed with or by something, it is surrounded by it.","ex":{"en":"The areas are sealed off and ringed by troops.","cn":"这些地区被军队封锁包围了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"给(鸟儿)环志","en":"If you ring a bird, you put a small metal ring around its leg so that you can identify it and study its movements and habits.","ex":{"en":"He demonstrated his techniques for ringing birds.","cn":"他展示了给鸟儿环志的技术。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"大大胜过;远远超过","en":"If you say that someone runs rings round you or runs rings around you, you mean that they are a lot better or a lot more successful than you at a particular activity.","ex":{"en":"Mentally, he can still run rings round men half his age!","cn":"他在智力上仍远远高于那些比他年轻一半的人。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"His name rings a bell but I can't think where we met.","cn":"他的名字听着很熟，但我想不起我们在哪里见过。"},{"en":"It may seem a strange story but it rings true to me.","cn":"这个故事也许显得离奇，但我却觉得很真实。"}]},"ritual":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ritual__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ritual__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪtʃuəl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a series of actions that are always performed in the same way, especially as part of a religious ceremony","cn":"程序；仪规；礼节；（尤指）宗教仪式","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"religious rituals","cn":"宗教仪式"}},{"en":"something that is done regularly and always in the same way","cn":"习惯；老规矩","ex":{"en":"Sunday lunch with the in-laws has become something of a ritual.","cn":"星期天和姻亲们共进午餐已经成了例行的公事。"}},{"en":"done as part of a ritual or ceremony","cn":"仪式上的；庆典的","ex":{"en":"ritual chanting","cn":"礼仪上的圣咏演唱"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"always done or said in the same way, especially when this is not sincere","cn":"老套的；例行公事的","ex":{"en":"ritual expressions of sympathy","cn":"例行公事地表示同情"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"典礼;(宗教)仪式","en":"A ritual is a religious service or other ceremony which involves a series of actions performed in a fixed order.","ex":{"en":"This is the most ancient, and holiest of the Shinto rituals","cn":"这是最古老、最神圣的神道教仪式。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"仪式性的;传统的","en":"Ritual activities happen as part of a ritual or tradition.","ex":{"en":"...fastings and ritual dancing.","cn":"斋戒和传统舞蹈"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"风俗;习惯","en":"A ritual is a way of behaving or a series of actions which people regularly carry out in a particular situation, because it is their custom to do so.","ex":{"en":"The whole Italian culture revolves around the ritual of eating","cn":"整个意大利的文化都以饮食习惯为中心。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"例行公事般的;习惯性的;老规矩的","en":"You can describe something as a ritual action when it is done in exactly the same way whenever a particular situation occurs.","ex":{"en":"I realized that here the conventions required me to make the ritual noises.","cn":"我意识到此时按照惯例我应该说些客套话。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Sunday lunch with the in-laws has become something of a ritual.","cn":"星期天和姻亲们共进午餐已经成了例行的公事。"},{"en":"She objects to the ritual of organized religion.","cn":"她反对有组织宗教的仪规。"}]},"rib":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rib__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rib__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/skeleton.jpg"]},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪb","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"any of the curved bones that are connected to the spine and surround the chest","cn":"肋骨","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a broken/bruised/cracked rib","cn":"折断的／挫伤的／开裂的肋骨"}},{"en":"a piece of meat with one or more bones from the ribs of an animal","cn":"排骨","g":"[uncountable, countable]"},{"en":"a curved piece of wood, metal or plastic that forms the frame of a boat, roof, etc. and makes it stronger","cn":"（船、屋顶等的）肋拱，肋材","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a roof with rib vaulting","cn":"带有肋拱顶的屋顶"}},{"en":"a way of knitting (= making clothing using wool and two long needles) that produces a pattern of straight lines up and down in which some are raised higher than others","cn":"凸条花纹编织；罗纹编织","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"a rib cotton sweater","cn":"一件罗纹棉毛衫"}},{"en":"to laugh at somebody and make jokes about them, but in a friendly way","cn":"嘲笑；逗弄；开（某人的）玩笑","ex":{"en":"He used to rib her mercilessly about her accent.","cn":"他常常因为她的口音而无情地取笑她。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"肋骨","en":"Your ribs are the 12 pairs of curved bones that surround your chest.","ex":{"en":"Her heart was thumping against her ribs","cn":"她的心脏紧抵着肋骨砰砰跳动。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"排骨;肋条（肉）","en":"A rib of meat such as beef or pork is a piece that has been cut to include one of the animal's ribs.","ex":{"en":"...a rib of beef.","cn":"牛排"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"罗纹针织法","en":"Rib is a method of knitting that makes a raised pattern of parallel lines. You use rib, for example, round the edge of sweaters so that the material can stretch without losing its shape."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"（友善地）开…的玩笑，逗弄，取笑","en":"If you rib someone about something, you tease them about it in a friendly way.","ex":{"en":"The guys in my local pub used to rib me about drinking 'girly' drinks.","cn":"我家当地酒馆里的人以前总是取笑我喝“女人”饮料。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Stop poking me in the ribs!","cn":"别捅我的腰！"},{"en":"a broken/bruised/cracked rib","cn":"折断的/挫伤的/断裂的肋骨"}]},"ridge":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ridge__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ridge__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪdʒ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a narrow area of high land along the top of a line of hills; a high pointed area near the top of a mountain","cn":"山脊；山脉","ex":{"en":"walking along the ridge","cn":"沿着山脊行走"}},{"en":"a raised line on the surface of something; the point where two sloping surfaces join","cn":"隆起；脊；垄","ex":{"en":"The ridges on the soles of my boots stopped me from slipping.","cn":"我靴子底上有隆起的纹路，使我没有滑倒。"}},{"en":"a long narrow area of high pressure in the atmosphere","cn":"（大气层的）高压脊","g":"[usually singular]","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"a ridge of high pressure over the Atlantic","cn":"大西洋上空的高压脊"}},{"en":"to make narrow raised lines or areas on the surface of something","cn":"使隆起；使形成脊状","pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"脊;山脊;山脉","en":"A ridge is a long, narrow piece of raised land."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(平面上的)隆起，脊，垄","en":"A ridge is a raised line on a flat surface.","ex":{"en":"...the bony ridge of the eye socket.","cn":"眼窝处突出的骨骼"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The ridges on the soles of my boots stopped me from slipping.","cn":"我靴子底上有隆起的纹路，使我没有滑倒。"},{"en":"the north-east ridge of Mount Everest","cn":"珠穆朗玛峰的东北部"}]},"rightly":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rightly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rightly__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪtli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"for a good reason","cn":"正当地；理由充分地","ex":{"en":"The school was rightly proud of the excellent exam results.","cn":"学校为这次出色的考试成绩感到骄傲，这是理所当然的。"}},{"en":"in a correct or accurate way","cn":"正确地；恰当地；精确地","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"As she rightly pointed out, the illness can affect adults as well as children.","cn":"她说得对，这种病不仅影响儿童，也会影响成年人。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The school was rightly proud of the excellent exam results.","cn":"学校为这次出色的考试成绩感到骄傲，这是理所当然的。"},{"en":"As she rightly pointed out, the illness can affect adults as well as children.","cn":"她说得对，这种病不仅影响儿童，也会影响成年人。"}]},"river":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/river__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/river__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪvə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a natural flow of water that continues in a long line across land to the sea","cn":"河；江","ex":{"en":"Eventually we came to the mouth of the River Thames.","cn":"最后，我们来到了泰晤士河的入海口。"}},{"en":"a large amount of liquid that is flowing in a particular direction","cn":"（液体）涌流","ex":{"en":"Rivers of molten lava flowed down the mountain.","cn":"大量的熔岩顺着山坡流下来。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"河;江","en":"A river is a large amount of fresh water flowing continuously in a long line across the land.","ex":{"en":"...a chemical works on the banks of the river.","cn":"跨河而建的一家化工厂"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Rivers of molten lava flowed down the mountain.","cn":"大量的熔岩顺着山坡流下来。"},{"en":"Can we swim in the river?","cn":"我们可以下河游泳吗？"}]},"ridiculous":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ridiculous__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ridiculous__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪˈdɪkjələs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very silly or unreasonable","cn":"愚蠢的；荒谬的；荒唐的","ex":{"en":"I look ridiculous in this hat.","cn":"我戴这顶帽子看上去很可笑。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"愚蠢的;荒谬的;可笑的","en":"If you say that something or someone is ridiculous, you mean that they are very foolish.","ex":{"en":"It is ridiculous to suggest we are having a romance","cn":"暗示我们正在谈恋爱的说法真是太荒谬了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Don't be ridiculous! You can't pay £50 for a T-shirt!","cn":"别犯傻了！你不会花 50 英镑买一件 T 恤衫的！"},{"en":"I look ridiculous in this hat.","cn":"我戴这顶帽子看上去很可笑。"}]},"risking":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪsk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the possibility of sth bad happening at some time in the future; a situation that could be dangerous or have a bad result","cn":"危险；风险"},{"en":"a person or thing that is likely to cause problems or danger at some time in the future","cn":"危险人物；会带来风险的事物"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/risk__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/risk__us_1.mp3"}},"ridiculously":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ridiculously__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ridiculously__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"荒唐地;荒谬地;可笑地;令人惊奇地","en":"You use ridiculously to emphasize the fact that you think something is unreasonable or very surprising.","ex":{"en":"Dena bought rolls of silk that seemed ridiculously cheap","cn":"德娜买了几卷看起来非常次的丝绸。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The meal was ridiculously expensive.","cn":"这顿饭贵得离谱。"},{"en":"That’s a ridiculous idea!","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"rɪˈdɪkjələsli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"to a silly or unreasonable degree","cn":"愚蠢的；荒谬的；荒唐的","ex":{"en":"The meal was ridiculously expensive.","cn":"这顿饭贵得离谱。"}}]}},"ribs":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪb","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"any of the curved bones that are connected to the spine and surround the chest","cn":"肋骨"},{"en":"a piece of meat with one or more bones from the ribs of an animal","cn":"排骨"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rib__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rib__us_1.mp3"}},"risk":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/risk__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/risk__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪsk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the possibility of something bad happening at some time in the future; a situation that could be dangerous or have a bad result","cn":"危险；风险","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The health risks are very low.","cn":"健康风险很低。"}},{"en":"a person or thing that is likely to cause problems or danger at some time in the future","cn":"危险人物；会带来风险的事物","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Those old boxes in the corridor are a fire risk.","cn":"走廊里的那些旧箱子有失火的危险。"}},{"en":"a person or business that a bank or an insurance company is willing/unwilling to lend money or sell insurance to because they are likely/unlikely to pay back the money, etc.","cn":"（风险很小／很大的）借款人，保险对象","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"With five previous claims, he's now a bad insurance risk.","cn":"由于已有了五次索赔要求，他现在是一位风险很大的被保险人。"}},{"en":"to put something valuable or important in a dangerous situation, in which it could be lost or damaged","cn":"面临危险；使处于危险境地","ex":{"en":"He risked his life to save her.","cn":"他冒着生命危险去救她。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to do something that may mean that you get into a situation which is unpleasant or harmful for you","cn":"冒…的风险（或危险）","ex":{"en":"There was no choice. If they stayed there, they risked death.","cn":"他们别无选择。如果待在那儿，就面临死亡。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to do something that you know is not really a good idea or may not succeed","cn":"冒险做；（明知结果而）大胆做","ex":{"en":"He risked a glance at her furious face.","cn":"他壮着胆子瞅了瞅她那张愤怒的脸。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"风险;危险","en":"If there is a risk of something unpleasant, there is a possibility that it will happen.","ex":{"en":"There is a small risk of brain damage from the procedure","cn":"该手术有导致脑损伤的轻微风险。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"有风险的事","en":"If something that you do is a risk, it might have unpleasant or undesirable results.","ex":{"en":"You're taking a big risk showing this to Kravis","cn":"你把这个给克拉维斯看会有很大的风险。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"冒险行为;威胁;隐患;危险的人","en":"If you say that something or someone is a risk, you mean they are likely to cause harm.","ex":{"en":"It's being overfat that constitutes a health risk","cn":"威胁健康的一个因素是身体过于肥胖。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"贷款对象;赊销对象","en":"If you are considered a good risk, a bank or shop thinks that it is safe to lend you money or let you have goods without paying for them at the time.","ex":{"en":"Before providing the cash, they will have to decide whether you are a good or bad risk","cn":"在提供资金之前，他们得确认你是不是信誉良好的贷款对象。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"冒着…的危险;担着…的风险","en":"If you risk something unpleasant, you do something which might result in that thing happening or affecting you.","ex":{"en":"Those who fail to register risk severe penalties","cn":"那些没有注册的人可能会受到严厉的处罚。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"冒险(做…)","en":"If you risk doing something, you do it, even though you know that it might have undesirable consequences.","ex":{"en":"The captain was not willing to risk taking his ship through the straits in such bad weather.","cn":"船长不愿意在这样恶劣的天气里冒险将船驶过海峡。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"冒着（失去生命等）的危险","en":"If you risk your life or something else important, you behave in a way that might result in it being lost or harmed.","ex":{"en":"She risked her own life to help a disabled woman","cn":"她冒着生命危险去帮助一个残疾妇女。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"处境危险;有风险的;在危险中","en":"To be at risk means to be in a situation where something unpleasant might happen.","ex":{"en":"Up to 25,000 jobs are still at risk","cn":"多达25,000份工作仍受到威胁。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"冒着…危险;担着…的风险","en":"If you do something at the risk of something unpleasant happening, you do it even though you know that the unpleasant thing might happen as a result.","ex":{"en":"At the risk of being repetitive, I will say again that statistics are only a guide","cn":"尽管会显得啰唆，但我还得再说一遍，统计数字只是一个参考。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"自担风险;责任自负;后果自负","en":"If you tell someone that they are doing something at their own risk, you are warning them that, if they are harmed, it will be their own responsibility.","ex":{"en":"Those who wish to come here will do so at their own risk.","cn":"那些想来这里的人风险自负。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"冒着…危险","en":"If you run the risk of doing or experiencing something undesirable, you do something knowing that the undesirable thing might happen as a result.","ex":{"en":"The officers had run the risk of being dismissed","cn":"这些警官冒了被开除的风险。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to risk your neck→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"We could probably trust her with the information but it's just not worth the risk.","cn":"我们也许可以将这些资料托付给她，但实在不值得去承担这样的风险。"},{"en":"With five previous claims, he's now a bad insurance risk.","cn":"由于已有了五次索赔要求，他现在是一位风险很大的受保人。"}]},"rice":{"oxford":{"phon":"raɪs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"short, narrow white or brown grain grown on wet land in hot countries as food; the plant that produces this grain","cn":"大米；稻米；稻","ex":{"en":"a grain of rice","cn":"一粒大米"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"米;大米;稻米","en":"Rice consists of white or brown grains taken from a cereal plant. You cook rice and usually eat it with meat or vegetables.","ex":{"en":"...a meal consisting of chicken, rice and vegetables","cn":"有鸡肉、米饭和蔬菜的一顿饭"}}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/cereals_comp.jpg","media/thumb/rice.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/rice__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rice__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"brown rice (= without its outer covering removed)","cn":"糙米"},{"en":"boiled/steamed/fried rice","cn":"米饭；蒸饭；炒饭"}]},"rich":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rich__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rich__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"rɪtʃ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having a lot of money or property","cn":"富有的；富裕的","lab":"slang","sc":"with a lot of money","ex":{"en":"She's one of the richest women in the world.","cn":"她是世界上最富有的女人之一。"}},{"en":"people who have a lot of money or property","cn":"富人；有钱人","g":"[plural]","sc":"with a lot of money","ex":{"en":"It's a favourite resort for the rich and famous.","cn":"这是富人和名流最喜欢去度假的地方。"}},{"en":"producing a lot of wealth so that many of its people can live at a high standard","cn":"富庶的；富饶的","sc":"with a lot of money","ex":{"en":"the richest countries/economies/nations","cn":"最富有的国家／经济体／国家"}},{"en":"containing or providing a large supply of something","cn":"大量含有（或提供）","lab":"figurative","sc":"containing/providing something","ex":{"en":"Oranges are rich in vitamin C.","cn":"柑橘含有丰富的维生素 C。"}},{"en":"very interesting and full of variety","cn":"非常有趣的；丰富多彩的","sc":"full of variety","ex":{"en":"the region’s rich history and culture","cn":"这个地区丰富多彩的历史和文化"}},{"en":"containing a lot of fat, butter, eggs, etc. and making you feel full quickly","cn":"油腻的","sc":"food","ex":{"en":"a rich, creamy sauce","cn":"油腻的奶油沙司"}},{"en":"containing the substances that make it good for growing plants in","cn":"肥沃的；丰产的","sc":"soil","ex":{"en":"a rich, well-drained soil","cn":"排水性能好的沃土"}},{"en":"strong or deep; very beautiful or attractive","cn":"强烈的；深的；低沉的；诱人的","sc":"colours/sounds","ex":{"en":"rich dark reds","cn":"浓重的深红色"}},{"en":"expensive and beautiful","cn":"华丽而昂贵的","lab":"literary","sc":"expensive","ex":{"en":"The rooms were decorated with rich fabrics.","cn":"这些屋子装饰着华丽昂贵的织物。"}},{"en":"used to say that a criticism somebody makes is surprising and not reasonable, because they have the same fault","cn":"（表示某人所作的批评是无稽之谈，因为他们本身也有同样的问题）","lab":"especially British English, informal，，","sc":"criticism","ex":{"en":"Me? Lazy? That's rich, coming from you!","cn":"我？懒？真可笑，你自己也一样！"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"富裕的;有钱的;富有的","en":"A rich person has a lot of money or valuable possessions.","ex":{"en":"You're going to be a very rich man","cn":"你将会成为一个非常有钱的人。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"财富;财产","en":"Riches are valuable possessions or large amounts of money.","ex":{"en":"An Olympic gold medal can lead to untold riches for an athlete","cn":"一枚奥运金牌能给运动员带来无尽的财富。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(国家)富有的，富饶的","en":"A rich country has a strong economy and produces a lot of wealth, so many people who live there have a high standard of living.","ex":{"en":"There is hunger in many parts of the world, even in rich countries.","cn":"世界上很多地方，甚至在富有的国家里，都有人忍饥挨饿。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"资源","en":"If you talk about the earth's riches, you are referring to things that exist naturally in large quantities and that are useful and valuable, for example minerals, wood, and oil.","ex":{"en":"...Russia's vast natural riches.","cn":"俄罗斯丰富的自然资源"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"富含…的;含有大量…的","en":"If something is rich in a useful or valuable substance or is a rich source of it, it contains a lot of it.","ex":{"en":"Liver and kidney are particularly rich in vitamin A","cn":"肝脏和肾脏的维生素A含量尤其丰富。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(食物)油腻的","en":"Rich food contains a lot of fat or oil.","ex":{"en":"...the hearty, rich foods of Gascony","cn":"加斯科涅丰盛而油腻的食物"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(土地)肥沃的，丰饶的，富饶的","en":"Rich soil contains large amounts of substances that make it good for growing crops or flowers in.","ex":{"en":"Farmers grow rice in the rich soil.","cn":"农民们在肥沃的土地上种植稻子。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(矿藏等)丰富的，大量的","en":"A rich deposit of a mineral or other substance is a large amount of it.","ex":{"en":"...the country's rich deposits of the metal, lithium.","cn":"这个国家丰富的锂金属矿藏"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"充满（幽默感、创意等）的;（信息）丰富的","en":"If you say that something is a rich vein or source of something such as humour, ideas, or information, you mean that it can provide a lot of that thing.","ex":{"en":"The director discovered a rich vein of sentimentality","cn":"导演发现了一个丰富的情感源泉。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(气味)浓郁的，香浓的;(颜色)浓艳的，强烈的，鲜艳的;（声音）低沉的，浑厚的","en":"Rich smells are strong and very pleasant. Rich colours and sounds are deep and very pleasant.","ex":{"en":"...a rich and luxuriously perfumed bath essence.","cn":"香味浓郁的沐浴香精"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(生活或历史)丰富多彩的","en":"A rich life or history is one that is interesting because it is full of different events and activities.","ex":{"en":"A rich and varied cultural life is essential for this couple.","cn":"丰富多样的文化生活对这对夫妇而言至关重要。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(收藏或混合物)丰富的，各种各样的","en":"A rich collection or mixture contains a wide and interesting variety of different things.","ex":{"en":"Visitors can view a rich and colorful array of aquatic plants and animals","cn":"游客们可以看到一系列各种各样、色彩斑斓的水生动植物。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"不合情理的;荒谬的;荒唐的","en":"If you say that something a person says or does is rich, you are making fun of it because you think it is a surprising and inappropriate thing for them to say or do.","ex":{"en":"Gil says that women can't keep secrets. That's rich, coming from him, the professional sneak.","cn":"吉尔说女人不能保守秘密。这话从他这样一个整天打小报告的人嘴里说出来真是太荒谬了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"富得流油;一身铜臭味","en":"If you say that someone is filthy rich or stinking rich, you disapprove of them because they have a lot of money.","ex":{"en":"He's stinking rich, and with no more talent than he ever had before.","cn":"他现在已经有几个臭钱了，但仍然和以前一样没什么才能。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"It's a favourite resort for the rich and famous.","cn":"这是富人和名流最喜欢去度假的地方。"},{"en":"His novels are a rich source of material for the movie industry.","cn":"他的小说为电影业提供了大量素材。"}]},"rigid":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪdʒɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very strict and difficult to change","cn":"死板的；僵硬的","lab":"often disapproving","ex":{"en":"The curriculum was too narrow and too rigid.","cn":"课程设置过于狭窄和死板。"}},{"en":"not willing to change their ideas or behaviour","cn":"固执的；僵化的；一成不变的","lab":"often disapproving","ex":{"en":"rigid attitudes","cn":"固执的态度"}},{"en":"stiff and difficult to move or bend","cn":"坚硬的；不弯曲的；僵直的","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"a rigid support for the tent","cn":"帐篷坚硬的支柱"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(法律、制度或体系)严格的，刻板的，不可变更的","en":"Laws, rules, or systems that are rigid cannot be changed or varied, and are therefore considered to be rather severe.","ex":{"en":"Several colleges in our study have rigid rules about student conduct","cn":"在我们的研究中，有几所大学制定了严格的学生行为规则。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"固执的;顽固的;刻板的","en":"If you disapprove of someone because you think they are not willing to change their way of thinking or behaving, you can describe them as rigid .","ex":{"en":"She was a fairly rigid person who had strong religious views","cn":"她相当顽固，宗教观念极强。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"坚硬的;刚性的;不易弯曲的","en":"A rigid substance or object is stiff and does not bend, stretch, or twist easily.","ex":{"en":"...rigid plastic containers","cn":"坚硬的塑料容器"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(常因震惊或害怕)身体僵直的，不能动弹的，呆住的","en":"If someone goes rigid, their body becomes very straight and stiff, usually as a result of shock or fear.","ex":{"en":"I went rigid with shock","cn":"我惊得僵在那里。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rigid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rigid__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"His rigid adherence to the rules made him unpopular.","cn":"他对规则的刻板坚持使得他不受欢迎。"},{"en":"She sat upright, her body rigid with fear.","cn":"她直挺挺地坐着，吓得浑身发僵。"}]},"rigorous":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rigorous__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rigorous__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪɡərəs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"done carefully and with a lot of attention to detail","cn":"谨慎的；细致的；彻底的","ex":{"en":"a rigorous analysis","cn":"细致的分析"}},{"en":"demanding that particular rules, processes, etc. are strictly followed","cn":"严格的；严厉的","ex":{"en":"The work failed to meet their rigorous standards.","cn":"工作没有达到他们的严格标准。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(测试、系统或程序)严格的，严密的，缜密的","en":"A test, system, or procedure that is rigorous is very thorough and strict.","ex":{"en":"The selection process is based on rigorous tests of competence and experience.","cn":"选拔过程是基于对能力和经验的严格测试。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"一丝不苟的;严格的;谨慎的","en":"If someone is rigorous in the way that they do something, they are very careful and thorough.","ex":{"en":"He is rigorous in his control of expenditure.","cn":"他对支出控制得非常严格。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The country's press is rigorously controlled.","cn":"这个国家的新闻出版事业受到严格控制。"},{"en":"The work failed to meet their rigorous standards.","cn":"工作没有达到他们的严格标准。"}]},"ritually":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪtʃuəli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a special way, especially as part of a religious ceremony","cn":"仪式：以一种特殊的方式，特别是作为宗教仪式的一部分","ex":{"en":"The goat was ritually slaughtered.","cn":"山羊按照仪式宰杀了。"}},{"en":"regularly and always in the same way","cn":"习惯；老规矩","ex":{"en":"Every day I ritually check the local news sites.","cn":"我每天都会例行公事地查看当地的新闻网站。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ritually__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ritually__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The goat was ritually slaughtered.","cn":"山羊按照仪式宰杀了。"},{"en":"The police issued the usual ritual apology.","cn":""}]},"rickshaw":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rickshaw__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rickshaw__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪkʃɔː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small, light vehicle with two wheels used especially in some Asian countries to carry passengers. The rickshaw is pulled by somebody walking or riding a bicycle.","cn":"人力车；黄包车"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"黄包车;人力车","en":"A rickshaw is a simple vehicle that is used in Asia for carrying passengers. Some rickshaws are pulled by a man who walks or runs in front."}]}},"ride":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ride__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ride__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"raɪd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to sit on an animal, especially a horse, and control it as it moves","cn":"骑，驾驭（动物，尤指马）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"horse","ex":{"en":"I learnt to ride as a child.","cn":"我小时候就学会了骑马。"}},{"en":"to spend time riding a horse for pleasure","cn":"骑马（消遣）","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"British English","sc":"horse","ex":{"en":"How often do you go riding?","cn":"你多长时间骑一次马？"}},{"en":"to sit on and control a bicycle, motorcycle, etc.","cn":"骑；驾驶","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"bicycle/motorcycle","ex":{"en":"The boys were riding their bikes around the streets.","cn":"男孩子们骑着自行车在街上兜风。"}},{"en":"to travel in a vehicle, especially as a passenger","cn":"搭乘；乘坐","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"North American English","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"I walked back while the others rode in the car.","cn":"别人都乘车，而我是走回来的。"}},{"en":"to float or be supported on water or air","cn":"漂浮；飘浮","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"on water/air","ex":{"en":"We watched the balloon riding high above the fields.","cn":"我们看着气球高高地飘浮在田野上空。"}},{"en":"to go through or over an area on a horse, bicycle, etc.","cn":"（骑马、自行车等）穿越，翻越","g":"[transitive]","sc":"go through area","ex":{"en":"We rode the mountain trails.","cn":"我们骑着马走在山里的小路上。"}},{"en":"to criticize or tease somebody in an annoying way","cn":"数落；嘲弄","g":"[transitive]","lab":"North American English","sc":"criticize","ex":{"en":"Why is everybody riding me today?","cn":"怎么今天大家都拿我取笑？"}},{"en":"a short journey in a vehicle, on a bicycle, etc.","cn":"（乘车或骑车的）短途旅程","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"a train ride through beautiful countryside","cn":"乘火车穿越美丽乡村的旅程"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a free ride in a car, etc. to a place you want to get to","cn":"免费搭车；搭便车","lab":"North American English","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"She hitched a ride to the station.","cn":"她搭便车去车站。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"the kind of journey you make in a car, etc.","cn":"（乘坐汽车等的）旅行","lab":"figurative","sc":"in vehicle","ex":{"en":"a smooth/comfortable/bumpy ride","cn":"平稳／舒适／颠簸的旅行"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a short journey on a horse, etc.","cn":"（骑马等的）短途旅程","sc":"on horse","ex":{"en":"There were pony rides for the children.","cn":"孩子们可以骑小马。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a large machine at a funfair or amusement park that you ride on for fun or excitement; an occasion when you go on one of these","cn":"供乘骑的游乐设施；乘坐（游乐设施）","sc":"at funfair","ex":{"en":"The rides are free.","cn":"免费乘坐。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"骑(马)","en":"When you ride a horse, you sit on it and control its movements.","ex":{"en":"I saw a girl riding a horse","cn":"我看见一个骑马的女孩。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"骑(自行车或摩托车)；驾驶","en":"When you ride a bicycle or a motorcycle, you sit on it, control it, and travel along on it.","ex":{"en":"Riding a bike is great exercise","cn":"骑自行车是很好的运动。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"搭乘,乘坐(交通工具)","en":"When you ride in a vehicle such as a car, you travel in it.","ex":{"en":"He prefers travelling on the Tube to riding in a limousine","cn":"他更愿意乘地铁出行，不愿坐豪华轿车。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(骑马、骑自行车或乘车的)旅行，旅程;车程","en":"A ride is a journey on a horse or bicycle, or in a vehicle.","ex":{"en":"She took some friends for a ride in the family car","cn":"她开着自己的家庭轿车载着几个朋友出去兜了一圈。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(游乐场中)供骑乘的游乐设施","en":"In a fairground, a ride is a large machine that people ride on for fun."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"依赖;依靠;取决于","en":"If you say that one thing is riding on another, you mean that the first thing depends on the second thing.","ex":{"en":"Billions of pounds are riding on the outcome of the election","cn":"几十亿英镑都取决于这次选举的结果。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"人气高涨;春风得意","en":"If you say that someone or something is riding high, you mean that they are popular or successful at the present time.","ex":{"en":"He was riding high in the public opinion polls","cn":"他在民意调查中支持率颇高。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"难题;非难;困境","en":"If you say that someone faces a rough ride, you mean that things are going to be difficult for them because people will criticize them a lot or treat them badly.","ex":{"en":"The Chancellor could face a rough ride unless the plan works","cn":"除非这个计划能够奏效，否则财政大臣将举步维艰。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"上当受骗;被欺骗","en":"If you say that someone has been taken for a ride, you mean that they have been deceived or cheated.","ex":{"en":"When he had not returned with my money an hour later I realized that I had been taken for a ride.","cn":"1个小时后他没有带着我的钱回来，我才意识到自己上当受骗了。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to ride roughshod over→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：ride out ride up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"We managed to get a ride into town when we missed the bus.","cn":"我们没赶上公共汽车，就设法搭了一辆便车去城里。"},{"en":"The band is riding the crest of its last tour.","cn":"乐队正处于最近这次巡回演出后的顶峰状态。"}]},"rival":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rival__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rival__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪvl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person, company or thing that competes with another in sport, business, etc.","cn":"竞争对手","ex":{"en":"The two teams have always been rivals.","cn":"这两个队一直是竞争对手。"}},{"en":"competing with another person, company, thing, etc.","cn":"相互竞争的；对抗的","ex":{"en":"a rival bid/claim/offer","cn":"竞争投标；对立的权利要求；竞争的出价"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"to be as good, impressive, etc. as somebody/something else","cn":"与…相匹敌；比得上","ex":{"en":"You will find scenery to rival anything you can see in the Alps.","cn":"你看到的景色可与你在阿尔卑斯山所看到的景色相媲美。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"竞争者;对手;敌手","en":"Your rival is a person, business, or organization who you are competing or fighting against in the same area or for the same things.","ex":{"en":"The world champion finished more than two seconds ahead of his nearest rival","cn":"世界冠军领先第二名2秒多钟到达终点。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"没有敌手;独一无二;无人能及","en":"If you say that someone or something has no rivals or is without rival, you mean that it is best of its type.","ex":{"en":"...a wonderfully fragrant wine which has no rivals in the Rhone","cn":"在罗纳河地区独一无二的无比香醇的葡萄酒"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"能与…媲美;与…匹敌;与…不分高低","en":"If you say that one thing rivals another, you mean that they are both of the same standard or quality.","ex":{"en":"Cassette recorders cannot rival the sound quality of CDs","cn":"卡式磁带录音机的音质无法和CD相媲美。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"You will find scenery to rival anything you can see in the Alps.","cn":"你看到的景色可与你在阿尔卑斯山所看到的景色相媲美。"},{"en":"The Japanese are our biggest economic rivals.","cn":"日本人是我们最大的经济竞争对手。"}]},"riders":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪdə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who rides a horse, bicycle or motorcycle","cn":"骑手；骑马（或自行车、摩托车）的人"},{"en":"an extra piece of information that is added to an official document","cn":"公文的附加材料；附文"}]}},"rivalry":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/rivalry__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/rivalry__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪvlri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a state in which two people, companies, etc. are competing for the same thing","cn":"竞争；竞赛；较量","ex":{"en":"a fierce rivalry for world supremacy","cn":"夺取世界霸权的激烈竞争"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"竞争;敌对","en":"Rivalry is competition or fighting between people, businesses, or organizations who are in the same area or want the same things.","ex":{"en":"...the rivalry between the Inkatha and the ANC","cn":"英卡塔自由党和非洲国民大会之间的敌对"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"There is a certain amount of friendly rivalry between the teams.","cn":"两队间有某种程度上的友好较量。"},{"en":"a fierce rivalry for world supremacy","cn":"夺取世界霸权的激烈竞争"}]},"ridden":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/ridden__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/ridden__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪdn","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"full of a particular unpleasant thing","cn":"充满（某种不良事物）的；满是…的","ex":{"en":"a disease-ridden slum","cn":"疾病流行的贫民窟"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She was guilt-ridden at the way she had treated him.","cn":"她为过去曾那样对待他而深感内疚。"},{"en":"She was ridden with guilt.","cn":"她深感歉疚。"}],"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Ridden is the past participle of ride."}]}},"riotously":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/riotously__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/riotously__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪətəsli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"extremely","cn":"极端；非常；极其","ex":{"en":"riotously funny","cn":"滑稽至极"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"riotously funny","cn":"滑稽至极"},{"en":"Their riotous behaviour led to their arrest.","cn":""}]},"rioters":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪət","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which a group of people behave in a violent way in a public place, often as a protest","cn":"暴乱；骚乱"},{"en":"( formal ) a collection of a lot of different types of the same thing","cn":"丰富多彩；品种繁多"}]}},"risks":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪsk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the possibility of sth bad happening at some time in the future; a situation that could be dangerous or have a bad result","cn":"危险；风险"},{"en":"a person or thing that is likely to cause problems or danger at some time in the future","cn":"危险人物；会带来风险的事物"}]}},"risen":{"oxford":{"phon":"raɪz","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an increase in an amount, a number or a level （","cn":"数量或水平的）增加，提高"},{"en":"an increase in the money you are paid for the work you do","cn":"加薪；工资增长"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Risen is the past participle of rise."}]}},"rises":{"oxford":{"phon":"raɪz","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an increase in an amount, a number or a level （","cn":"数量或水平的）增加，提高"},{"en":"an increase in the money you are paid for the work you do","cn":"加薪；工资增长"}]}},"richest":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪtʃ","pos":"adj.","senses":[{"en":"having a lot of money or property","cn":"富有的；富裕的"},{"en":"people who have a lot of money or property","cn":"富人；有钱人"}]}},"rivers":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪvə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a natural flow of water that continues in a long line across land to the sea/ocean","cn":"河；江"},{"en":"a large amount of liquid that is flowing in a particular direction （","cn":"液体）涌流"}]}},"rigor":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪɡə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of being careful and paying great attention to detail","cn":"谨慎；缜密；严谨"},{"en":"( formal ) the fact of being strict or severe","cn":"严格；严厉"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/rigor0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/rigor.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"}]}},"rights":{"oxford":{"phon":"raɪt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"morally good or acceptable; correct according to law or a person's duty","cn":"正当；妥当"},{"en":"true or correct as a fact","cn":"正确的；真正的；真实的"}]}},"rivulets":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪvjələt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a very small river; a small stream of water or other liquid","cn":"小河；小溪；溪流；细流"}]}},"ripped":{"oxford":{"phon":"rɪpt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"badly torn","cn":"破烂不堪的","ex":{"en":"She wore a pair of faded, ripped blue jeans.","cn":"她穿了一条退色的带破洞的蓝色牛仔裤。"}},{"en":"having strong muscles that you can see clearly","cn":"有明显肌肉线条的","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"I'm not trying to get ripped—I just want to stay fit.","cn":"我不想练出肌肉线条，我只想保持健康。"}}]}},"rickshaws":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪkʃɔː","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small light vehicle with two wheels used in some Asian countries to carry passengers. The rickshaw is pulled by sb walking or riding a bicycle.","cn":"人力车；黄包车"}]}},"rituals":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪtʃuəl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a series of actions that are always performed in the same way, especially as part of a religious ceremony","cn":"程序；仪规；礼节；（尤指）宗教仪式"},{"en":"something that is done regularly and always in the same way","cn":"习惯；老规矩"}]}},"riots":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪət","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a situation in which a group of people behave in a violent way in a public place, often as a protest","cn":"暴乱；骚乱"},{"en":"( formal ) a collection of a lot of different types of the same thing","cn":"丰富多彩；品种繁多"}]}},"ripple":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"波纹;涟漪;细浪","en":"Ripples are little waves on the surface of water caused by the wind or by something moving in or on the water."},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)泛起涟漪;(使)泛起细浪","en":"When the surface of an area of water ripples or when something ripples it, a number of little waves appear on it.","ex":{"en":"You throw a pebble in a pool and it ripples","cn":"往池塘里扔块鹅卵石就会激起一片涟漪。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(植物等)如波浪起伏;（使）呈波状起伏","en":"When the wind ripples plants or trees or when they ripple, they move in a wave-like motion.","ex":{"en":"A slight wind rippled the crops in the valley","cn":"一阵微风吹过，山谷里的庄稼便随风起伏。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(感觉)传开，传遍","en":"If something such as a feeling ripples over someone's body, it moves across it or through it.","ex":{"en":"A chill shiver rippled over his skin.","cn":"他浑身打了个冷战。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(事情引起的)连锁反应，涟漪作用","en":"If an event causes ripples, its effects gradually spread, causing several other events to happen one after the other.","ex":{"en":"The ripples of Europe's currency crisis continue to be felt in most of the member states","cn":"欧洲货币危机引起的连锁反应仍在影响着大多数的成员国。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to move in small waves, or to make something move in this way （","cn":"使）起涟漪﹐（使）起细浪"},{"en":"to pass from one person to another like a wave 〔","cn":"在人群中〕传开"},{"en":"if a feeling ripples through you, you feel it strongly 〔","cn":"情感〕传遍﹐涌起"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n v 2 n","senses":[{"en":"A ripple is a small wave on the surface of something, such as a ripple that forms a ring around the spot where you threw a pebble into the pond."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. gently, smoothly, softly","PREP. across Small waves rippled gently across the pond. | through Shock rippled through her."]},"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/ripples.jpg"],"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/ripple_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/e/ripple1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The air was so still that there was hardly a ripple on the pond's surface.","cn":"空气静止不动，池塘的水面上几乎看不到波纹。"},{"en":"The announcement sent a ripple of excitement through the crowd.","cn":"这件事一宣布就在人群里引起了一阵兴奋。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪpl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a small wave on the surface of a liquid, especially water in a lake, etc.","cn":"波纹；细浪；涟漪","ex":{"en":"The air was so still that there was hardly a ripple on the pond's surface.","cn":"空气静止不动，池塘的水面上几乎看不到波纹。"}},{"en":"a thing that looks or moves like a small wave","cn":"（外观或运动）如波纹的东西","ex":{"en":"ripples of sand","cn":"沙滩上的波纹"}},{"en":"a sound that gradually becomes louder and then quieter again","cn":"起伏的声音","g":"[usually singular]","ex":{"en":"a ripple of applause/laughter","cn":"一阵阵的掌声／笑声"}},{"en":"a feeling that gradually spreads through a person or group of people","cn":"逐渐扩散的感觉","g":"[usually singular]","ex":{"en":"A ripple of fear passed through him.","cn":"一股恐惧感传遍了他的全身。"}},{"en":"to move or to make something move in very small waves","cn":"（使）如波浪般起伏","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"The sea rippled and sparkled.","cn":"大海波光粼粼。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to spread through a person or a group of people like a wave","cn":"扩散；涌起","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"A gasp rippled through the crowd.","cn":"人群中传出一片惊诧之声。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"ripe":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(水果、谷物等)成熟的","en":"Ripe fruit or grain is fully grown and ready to eat.","ex":{"en":"Always choose firm, but ripe fruit.","cn":"一定要挑选硬实但已成熟的水果。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(时机)成熟的，适宜的","en":"If a situation is ripe for a particular development or event, you mean that development or event is likely to happen soon.","ex":{"en":"Conditions were ripe for an outbreak of cholera","cn":"霍乱即将暴发。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(活到)高龄","en":"If someone lives to a ripe old age, they live until they are very old.","ex":{"en":"He lived to the ripe old age of 95.","cn":"他活到了95岁高龄。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"唾手可得;得到…易如反掌","en":"If something is ripe for picking or ripe for plucking, it will be very easy to obtain.","ex":{"en":"Haig's message was that victory was ripe for picking.","cn":"黑格传达的意思是说胜利唾手可得。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"时机已经成熟","en":"If you say the time is ripe, you mean that a suitable time has arrived for something to be done.","ex":{"en":"He told reporters that he thought the time was ripe for a normalisation of relations","cn":"他告诉记者他认为是时候恢复两国间正常关系。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having done everything that needs to be done in order to prepare for something","cn":""},{"en":"ready to deal with a situation, because you are expecting it or have made careful preparations","cn":""},{"en":"to be ready to start doing something that you have planned to do, and be just about to do it","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"When a fruit is ripe , it is time to pick it and eat it. If you say the time is ripe , then now is the time for action. Ripe means ready."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel, look, smell, taste","ADV. really, very a really ripe strawberry | fully, perfectly, quite Make sure the plums are fully ripe before you eat them . Some of the ap"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/ripe0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/ripe.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Reforms were promised when the time was ripe.","cn":"曾经作出承诺，时机一成熟就进行改革。"},{"en":"He lived to the ripe old age of 91.","cn":"他活到了 91 岁的高龄。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"raɪp","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"fully grown and ready to be eaten","cn":"成熟的","ex":{"en":"Pick the tomatoes before they get too ripe.","cn":"在西红柿太熟之前采摘它们。"}},{"en":"having a taste that has fully developed","cn":"口味浓郁的；成熟的；醇美可口的"},{"en":"strong and unpleasant","cn":"强烈的；难闻的"},{"en":"ready or suitable for something to happen","cn":"时机成熟的；适宜的","ex":{"en":"This land is ripe for development.","cn":"这片土地适宜开发。"}}]}},"rigour":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"困难;艰苦;严苛;严峻","en":"If you refer to the rigours of an activity or job, you mean the difficult, demanding, or unpleasant things that are associated with it.","ex":{"en":"He found the rigours of the tour too demanding.","cn":"他发现这次旅行非常艰苦。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"严格;严密;缜密","en":"If something is done with rigour, it is done in a strict, thorough way.","ex":{"en":"The new current affairs series promises to address challenging issues with freshness and rigour.","cn":"新的时事系列节目承诺以全新的视角和严谨的态度谈论有挑战性的问题。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the problems and difficulties of a situation","cn":"某事物的严酷[艰苦]"},{"en":"great care and thoroughness in making sure that something is correct","cn":"严密﹐缜密﹐严谨"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. full The crime will be treated with the full rigour of the law. | academic, intellectual, logical, scientific","VERB + RIGOUR lack Their analysis lacks rigour.","PREP. with ~ | ~ in There is a need for academic rigour in approaching this problem. 2 rigours: severe conditions","ADJ. full","VERB + RIGOUR be subjected to, face, suffer computers that are subjected to the rigours of the office environment | avoid, escape The town m"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/rigor0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/rigor.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The plants were unable to withstand the rigours of a harsh winter.","cn":"这些植物经受不住严冬的考验。"},{"en":"This crime must be treated with the full rigour of the law.","cn":"这一罪行必须严格依法审理。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪɡə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the fact of being careful and paying great attention to detail","cn":"谨慎；缜密；严谨","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"academic/intellectual/scientific, etc. rigour","cn":"学术、思想、科学等方面的严谨"}},{"en":"the fact of being strict or severe","cn":"严格；严厉","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"This crime must be treated with the full rigour of the law.","cn":"这一罪行必须严格依法审理。"}},{"en":"the difficulties and unpleasant conditions of something","cn":"艰苦；严酷","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"The plants were unable to withstand the rigours of a harsh winter.","cn":"这些植物经受不住严冬的考验。"}}]}},"rinse":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"清洗;冲洗","en":"When you rinse something, you wash it in clean water in order to remove dirt or soap from it.","ex":{"en":"After shampooing, always rinse the hair several times in clear water","cn":"每次用完洗发剂后都要用清水将头发冲洗几次。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"漱（口）","en":"If you rinse your mouth, you wash it by filling your mouth with water or with a liquid that kills germs, then spitting it out.","ex":{"en":"Use a toothbrush on your tongue as well, and rinse your mouth frequently.","cn":"舌头也要用牙刷清洁，并且经常漱口。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"染发剂","en":"A hair rinse is a dye whose colour gradually disappears after you have washed your hair a number of times, rather than being permanent."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to remove dirt from something","cn":""},{"en":"to clean something with water and usually soap","cn":""},{"en":"to clean a surface with a cloth, often a wet cloth","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. good | final | cold","VERB + RINSE give sth Give your hair a good rinse after shampooing it.","PREP. ~ in/with a rinse with cold water"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/rinse_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/rinse1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Rinse the cooked pasta with boiling water.","cn":"将煮过的意大利面在沸水里过一下。"},{"en":"Fabric conditioner is added during the final rinse.","cn":"在最后一遍漂洗时加入织物柔顺剂。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"rɪns","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to wash something with clean water only, not using soap","cn":"（用清水）冲洗，洗涮","ex":{"en":"Rinse the cooked pasta with boiling water.","cn":"将煮过的意大利面在沸水里过一下。"}},{"en":"to remove the soap from something with clean water after washing it","cn":"冲掉…的皂液；漂洗；清洗","ex":{"en":"Always rinse your hair thoroughly.","cn":"每次都要彻底冲洗头发。"}},{"en":"to remove dirt, etc. from something by washing it with clean water","cn":"（用清水）冲掉，洗刷","ex":{"en":"She rinsed the mud from her hands.","cn":"她冲洗掉手上的泥浆。"}},{"en":"an act of rinsing something","cn":"漂洗；冲洗；洗刷","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"I gave the glass a rinse.","cn":"我把杯子冲洗了一下。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a liquid that you put on your hair when it is wet in order to change its colour","cn":"染发剂","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a blue rinse","cn":"蓝色染发剂"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a liquid used for cleaning the mouth and teeth","cn":"漱口液","g":"[countable, uncountable]","pos":"noun"}]}},"risky":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"危险的;有风险的","en":"If an activity or action is risky, it is dangerous or likely to fail.","ex":{"en":"Investing in airlines is a very risky business","cn":"投资航空业风险很大。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"likely to cause death or serious harm, or cause something bad to happen","cn":""},{"en":"if something is risky, something bad could easily happen or you could easily make a mistake","cn":""},{"en":"dangerous – used especially about substances, jobs, and journeys","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, look, prove, seem, sound | consider sth","ADV. decidedly, extremely, highly, very It all sounds decidedly risky to me. | increasingly | a bit, a little, quite, rather, somewhat | inh"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/risky0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/risky.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It's far too risky to generalize from one set of results.","cn":"仅根据一组结果进行概括是十分不可靠的。"},{"en":"Life as an aid worker can be a risky business (= dangerous).","cn":"救援人员的工作会有危险。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈrɪski","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"involving the possibility of something bad happening","cn":"有危险（或风险）的","ex":{"en":"Life as an aid worker can be a risky business (= dangerous).","cn":"救援人员的工作会有危险。"}}]}},"rifle":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"来复枪;步枪","en":"A rifle is a gun with a long barrel.","ex":{"en":"They shot him at point blank range with an automatic rifle","cn":"他们用自动步枪近距离开枪射杀了他。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"快速翻找;搜寻","en":"If you rifle through things or rifle them, you make a quick search among them in order to find something or steal something.","ex":{"en":"I discovered my husband rifling through the filing cabinet","cn":"我发现我丈夫正在档案柜里匆匆翻找着什么东西。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a long gun which you hold up to your shoulder to shoot","cn":"来复枪﹐步枪"},{"en":"to search a place or container quickly because you are looking for something, especially something to steal","cn":"迅速翻找〔尤指偷窃〕"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 v","senses":[{"en":"A rifle is a long, powerful gun that is fired from the shoulder. A soldier is most often armed with a rifle ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. automatic, high-powered, semi-automatic, .22 | air, army, assault, hunting, sporting | Kalashnikov, M-16, etc.","VERB + RIFLE load, reload | raise | aim | fire | shoot sb/sth with | be armed with, carry","RIFLE + NOUN barrel, butt | bullet | fire, shot | club, range"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/3/brelasderifle.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/rifle1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She rifled through her clothes for something suitable to wear.","cn":"她急匆匆地在衣服堆里找合适的衣服穿。"},{"en":"His wallet had been rifled.","cn":"他的钱包被偷了。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈraɪfl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a gun with a long barrel which you hold to your shoulder to fire","cn":"步枪；来复枪","ex":{"en":"a hunting rifle","cn":"猎枪"}},{"en":"to search quickly through something in order to find or steal something","cn":"快速搜寻；匆忙翻找","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"She rifled through her clothes for something suitable to wear.","cn":"她急匆匆地在衣服堆里找合适的衣服穿。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to steal something from somewhere","cn":"偷窃；盗取","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"His wallet had been rifled.","cn":"他的钱包被偷了。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to kick a ball very hard and straight in a game of football (soccer)","cn":"猛踢（足球）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"She rifled the ball into the roof of the net.","cn":"她将球射入网顶。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"rift":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(关系的)严重不和，裂痕，争议","en":"A rift between people or countries is a serious quarrel or disagreement that stops them having a good relationship.","ex":{"en":"The interview reflected a growing rift between the President and the government","cn":"这段采访反映了总统和政府之间的裂痕越来越大。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指地面的)裂缝，裂口","en":"A rift is a split that appears in something solid, especially in the ground."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"if an unpleasant situation or problem causes or leads to an argument , it makes people argue","cn":""},{"en":"if a bad situation or a problem comes between two people, it makes them argue, usually with the result that they stop being friends","cn":""},{"en":"if a bad situation, a problem etc causes a rift between two people, it makes them have a small argument with the result that they are not as friendly as they were before","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Rift sounds like rip, and it's helpful to think of it that way. When there is a rift in a political party over how much taxes to pay, it is like a rip or tear in the fabric of the group."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. deep, growing, serious | public | ideological | marital, marriage","VERB + RIFT cause, create, lead to | deepen, widen His actions only deepened the rift between himself and the majority of Congress. | heal, ","RIFT + VERB develop, occur, open up A rift had opened up within the party. | deepen, grow, widen","PREP. ~ among/between new evidence of a rift between the two countries | ~ in/within The debate has succeeded only in widening rifts within "]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/rift0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/rift.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Efforts to heal the rift between the two countries have failed.","cn":"弥合两国间分歧的各种努力都已失败。"},{"en":"The rift within the party deepened.","cn":"党内的分歧加深了。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"rɪft","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a serious break in the relationship between people or organizations","cn":"分裂；严重不和","lab":"US English","ex":{"en":"The rift within the party deepened.","cn":"党内的分歧加深了。"}},{"en":"a large break or opening in the ground, rocks or clouds","cn":"断裂；裂缝；裂口","ex":{"en":"Through a rift in the clouds we could see a beautiful blue sky.","cn":"透过云层的裂缝，我们可以看到美丽的蓝天。"}}]}}});
